   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access of South Tarawa&amp;apos;s population to safe, climate-resilient water supplies increased</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2028, at least 95% of South Tarawa&amp;apos;s population (51.5% of them women) has access to safe, climate-resilient water supplies (2019 baseline: &amp;lt;10%) 
Progress/Status: Current progress based on 4,666 households (equating to approximately 28,000 people or 44% of South Tarawa&amp;apos;s population [63,072] including an estimated 32,800 [52%] women and girls) are currently connected to the PUB water supply network with water supplied from the McKenzie
desalination plant. 
Data Source: PUB reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="10" year="2019"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2028-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2028-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="95"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
